# Installation

## Local path plugin

During development, load the plugin from a local checkout:

```json
{
  "plugin": ["/absolute/path/to/opencode-squad"]
}
```

Restart OpenCode after changing plugin code or bundled assets.

## Package plugin

Load the published package by package name:

```json
{
  "plugin": ["@geck-dev/opencode-squad@latest"]
}
```

You can omit `@latest` if you want OpenCode/npm resolution to use the default latest dist-tag:

```json
{
  "plugin": ["@geck-dev/opencode-squad"]
}
```

For reproducible setup, pin a concrete version instead of `@latest`:

```json
{
  "plugin": ["@geck-dev/opencode-squad@0.1.0"]
}
```

## Inline options

OpenCode plugin tuple options can override `squad.json` values for a specific OpenCode configuration file:

```json
{
  "plugin": [
    [
      "@geck-dev/opencode-squad",
      {
        "models": {
          "handlers": {
            "primary": "@provider/gpt"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  ]
}
```

Use tuple options sparingly. Prefer `squad.json` for settings that should be shared across sessions or projects.

## Next step

Continue with [Configuration](configuration.md) to set model handlers, primary-agent behavior, and local paths.

