# MCP servers

MCP servers are configured under `mcp` in `opencode.json`. They add tools to the model context, so keep enabled servers focused.

Local MCP:

```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "local_server": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["npx", "-y", "my-mcp-command"],
      "enabled": true,
      "environment": {}
    }
  }
}
```

Remote MCP:

```json
{
  "mcp": {
    "remote_server": {
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://mcp.example.com/mcp",
      "enabled": true,
      "headers": {}
    }
  }
}
```

Use environment references for secrets. Do not write literal API keys.

